Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) shouldn't stop you from thinking about pregnancy right now. The main thing is to stay healthy and not worry about the future. Since you haven't thought about pregnancy yet, there's no need to change your current lifestyle. Just enjoy yourself!

The idea that PCOS doesn't matter now is a very safe way to go about it. You won’t be thinking about anything else anyway. It’s really important that you don't change how you think about things just now. This is the best approach, and everything will be okay if you do nothing special.

As long as you’re living life normally, there’s absolutely no need to change your normal routine. Don’t put unnecessary pressure on yourself in these first few years! This is the easiest thing to do. After all, you won’t be thinking about the future, so you won’t feel any pressure about changing what you’re doing.

