Exercising late at night won’t affect your sleep; in fact, you might even feel more tired once you’re done exercising. Your body will eventually adjust to a routine of sleeping after working out. The key is to avoid any strenuous activities before bedtime; instead, wind down slowly and let your mind rest.

Inactivity is what makes you feel sleepy. It's just common sense to think that you'll get tired when you don't do anything for a while. There is no need to be concerned about it as long as you aren't active right before going to bed.

Sleep comes naturally after you stop doing things that stimulate you. Just relax and allow your body to catch up on its own. You'll find that your body will fall asleep when it deems appropriate. There is absolutely nothing to worry about.

Just ensure that you're not doing anything strenuous and everything will work out fine.

